  "body": "The second read of PR #3656 (merged as `2de071415`) found no blocker. These items stay open:\n\n- [ ] `confined` in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/adaptive_troch.rs` reads only the end points of a straight feed. A chord between two permitted points can cross a part of the keep-out. The post block (`verify_avoid`) catches it, so the result is a refusal late, not a collision. Check the full segment in the planner.\n- [ ] The tests in `crates/motion/tests/avoid_adaptive.rs` assert \"no hit\". Add one assert of the measured minimum distance between the swept tool and the item (not less than the clearance).\n- [ ] The test of the case with no room reads the refusal of `generate` only. The issue #3346 asks for a blocked post: read it in the test.\n- [ ] Find out if the Spiral method reports the area that it leaves uncut next to an item (the Trochoidal method adds a note with mm² and percent). Add the note if it is missing.\n- [ ] `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/do_not_touch.rs` has 407 lines. Split it under 400.\n\nRefs #3346, #3702.\n",
